# Local-only secrets for Doodle AI. Copy to .dev.vars and fill real values.
# In production these are set with `wrangler secret put <NAME>`.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cloudflare IDs (fill these in wrangler.json or pass as env vars)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=your-cf-account-id
# D1_DATABASE_ID=your-d1-database-uuid
# KV_NAMESPACE_ID=your-kv-namespace-id
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

OPENROUTER_API_KEY=replace-with-your-openrouter-key
# OpenRouter provider/model ID. The `openrouter/` gateway prefix is added by the app.
OPENROUTER_MODEL=google/gemini-3.7-flash

# Signing key for Better Auth sessions. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=replace-with-a-random-32-byte-base64-string

# Optional. Defaults to the request origin, which is correct for both
# `astro dev` and the deployed Worker. Set it only if the app is served
# behind a proxy that rewrites the origin.
# BETTER_AUTH_URL=https://doodleai.art

# Required — Google is the only sign-in method (see src/lib/auth/index.ts,
# which throws on startup if either is missing). Create credentials at
# https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials with the redirect URI
#   <origin>/api/auth/callback/google
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=replace-with-your-google-oauth-client-id
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=replace-with-your-google-oauth-client-secret

# Server-owned PicX key used for authenticated, credit-metered generation and uploads.
PICX_API_KEY=replace-with-a-picx-key

# Signing secret for inbound PicX webhook deliveries (X-PicX-Signature).
#
# ── WHY THIS IS NOT OPTIONAL FOR VIDEO ──────────────────────────────────────
# The async submit path is gated on this being set. While it is BLANK:
#   • image batches silently fall back to the OLD synchronous path (each render
#     blocks the request), which still works — so leaving it blank looks fine;
#   • POST /api/webhooks/picx refuses every delivery with 503 (fails closed);
#   • VIDEO has NO synchronous fallback — a clip is submitted async and completed
#     only by the inbound webhook, so with this blank VIDEO SIMPLY CANNOT WORK.
# It reads as "set but empty" today; that empty value is what disables video.
#
# ── HOW TO GET THE VALUE (format: whsec_<hex>) ──────────────────────────────
# Two sources, pick one:
#   1. Per-request callback_url (what this app uses): the signing secret is the
#      deterministic inline secret DERIVED FROM THE API KEY. Read it from the API
#      key's detail endpoint in the PicX developer console — it is shown as a
#      `whsec_`-prefixed value tied to that key and is stable for the key.
#   2. Registered webhook: create a webhook in the PicX console instead, which
#      issues its OWN `whsec_` secret — shown ONCE at creation, so copy it then.
# Do not invent one: an HMAC computed with the wrong secret fails every delivery
# (401 invalid_signature), which is indistinguishable from "not configured".
#
# ── WHERE IT BELONGS (project rule) ─────────────────────────────────────────
#   • Deployed Workers: Cloudflare Secrets Store, bound via secrets_store_secrets
#     in wrangler.json for BOTH prod and staging. Create the store secret FIRST,
#     THEN add the binding — a binding that references a missing secret fails the
#     deploy with error 10182 and blocks every later deploy of that worker,
#     including git-connected auto-deploys. See docs/secrets.md for the commands.
#   • Locally: this .dev.vars file only.
#   • NEVER in a tracked file, and NEVER as a PUBLIC_-prefixed build-time var —
#     it is a server-side signing key and must not reach the browser bundle.
#
# Local astro dev cannot receive real deliveries: PicX rejects a callback host it
# cannot resolve publicly, so localhost is not a usable target. Expose it with
# `cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:4321`, or exercise the verifier
# offline with `node scripts/video-smoke.mjs` (see that file's header).
PICX_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# tldraw canvas licence key. NOT actually secret — tldraw validates it in the
# browser, so it is served to every visitor as an island prop. It lives here (and
# in Secrets Store for deploys) because it must stay out of this public repo.
#
# Read per request from the Worker env via src/lib/tldraw-license.ts. It is NOT
# PUBLIC_-prefixed any more: that made it a build-time value baked into the JS
# bundle, so a Cloudflare build without .env silently shipped an undefined key.
#
# Without it the canvas mounts, works for about five seconds, then replaces
# itself with a hidden "licence expired" div — on any non-localhost origin. It
# does NOT merely watermark. localhost is exempt, which is what hid the fault.
# Get one at https://tldraw.dev/pricing
TLDRAW_LICENSE_KEY=replace-with-your-tldraw-license-key


# ── Local video/webhook testing over a tunnel ────────────────────────────────
#
# WHY THIS IS NEEDED. The callback URL PicX delivers results to is derived from
# the incoming request's origin, so staging and production each call themselves
# back with zero config. On a dev machine that derives http://localhost:4321,
# which PicX's SSRF guard refuses — so a video generation can never complete
# locally. Point the callback at a tunnel instead:
#
#   ngrok http --domain="intensely-moral-pig.ngrok-free.app" 4321
#
# Then the receiver is https://intensely-moral-pig.ngrok-free.app/api/webhooks/picx
#
# Leave PICX_CALLBACK_ORIGIN UNSET in staging and production. Set there it would
# route every environment's callbacks to one host, including production results
# to somebody's dev tunnel.
PICX_CALLBACK_ORIGIN=https://intensely-moral-pig.ngrok-free.app

# ── Signature verification: the part that cannot be skipped by choice ────────
#
# PicX SIGNS every delivery (X-PicX-Signature: t=…,v1=…). That is not optional on
# their side and there is no "unsigned" mode. Which secret it signs with depends
# on how the generation was submitted, and this is the bit that decides your setup:
#
#   callback_url only   -> signed with a secret DERIVED from your API key
#                          (HMAC of PicX's own server key + the api_key_id).
#                          No endpoint returns it, so a consumer CANNOT obtain it
#                          and therefore cannot verify these deliveries.
#   registered webhook  -> signed with that webhook's own whsec_… secret, which
#                          POST /api/webhooks returns EXACTLY ONCE. This is the
#                          only retrievable secret, and the only verifiable setup.
#
# So for a real environment: register a webhook in the PicX console, copy the
# whsec_ value here once, and submit generations bound to that webhook id.
PICX_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# DEV ONLY. Accepts UNVERIFIED deliveries when PICX_WEBHOOK_SECRET is empty, so
# you can test the full video round trip over ngrok before a webhook is
# registered. It disables the ONLY authentication on an endpoint that marks paid
# generations complete and writes media URLs into a user's gallery — while it is
# on, anyone who can reach your tunnel can forge a completion. Every accepted
# delivery logs a warning. Never set this in staging or production; a configured
# PICX_WEBHOOK_SECRET always wins over it.
PICX_WEBHOOK_INSECURE_DEV=false
